00:49:11.000 --> 00:49:41.000
even if it isn't the primary domain in which we are feeling stuck, can be helpful in unsticking us. Exactly. Yeah, I think the sense of movement, the sense of velocity is more important than what the velocity specifically and narrowly, concretely represents. It's just the feeling that you are not stagnant. Adam Alter is a psychologist at New York University. He is the author of the book, anatomy of a breakthrough, how to get unstuck when it matters most.

