01:33:13.000 --> 01:33:57.000
because maybe we'll return home to a quiet room or a quiet house and where the loss is still much more pervasive. We might take that time to allow ourselves to feel that pain a little bit more then. And that's very much what a lot of people do. Moray also points out that tragedies like the death of a child were a lot more common in the past. And it makes her think about how previous generations grappled with grief. So I guess, you know, on the one hand, it kind of like bonds me to mothers everywhere and kind of reminds me that this tragedy is very common. But it also kind of, it kind of leads me to think that like maybe we're a little too precious

